  "normalization": [
    "Every native item is a hand-authored projection, not a wire capture. Keys marked $synthetic represent non-serializable AsyncIterable input and unqualified SandboxSettings, canUseTool and SessionStore configuration. The success result text field is result: string in the pinned mirror.",
    "Session identity is observed from the message stream and bound in the adapter's private journal; the documented sessionId option selects a host-derived UUID that is distinct from the Strata task UUID and supplies no native deduplication or exactly-once guarantee.",
    "Request, result and artifact digests, snapshot sequences and terminal immutability are bridge-owned Strata execution/1 facts recomputed here with the shared helpers; the native interface supplies no equivalent guarantee.",
    "resume, forkSession and continue are never used by status or result: the session-storage documentation states resume re-spawns the agent and passes the ID to the subprocess, so resume creates new work rather than a read-only observation or loss recovery.",
    "query.interrupt is cooperative and only available in streaming input mode; an interrupt receipt listing cancelled items is not proof that this task stopped, and completion may still win the race, as scenario five illustrates.",
    "Every error after adapter invocation carries dispatch unknown; only a guard refusal before invocation could be not_dispatched, and none is illustrated. No native message text, environment, stack or credential enters a persisted error.",
    "Session metadata/history contain no terminal SDKResultMessage guarantee. Known-session recovery assumes a separately retained, attributable completion from the original query stream; history alone cannot establish success. Mirror writes are best-effort and history may be compacted.",
    "query.interrupt may resolve undefined; its receipt contains still_queued, not cancelled, because this method never sends cancel_queued. Receipt projections are method return values, not SDKMessage events."
  ],
